### Practical 9: In-Memory Caching & Latency Optimization REST Client
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000

### 1. Server Health Check & Cache Engine Metadata
GET {{baseUrl}}/
Accept: application/json

### 2. View Cache Statistics Initially (Supplementary Problem 2)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cache/stats
Accept: application/json

### 3. Clear/Flush In-Memory Cache (Supplementary Problem 2)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/cache/clear
Accept: application/json

### 4. Register New User
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Manan Vasani",
  "email": "cache_manan@charusat.edu.in",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 5. Login User & Retrieve JWT Token
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "cache_manan@charusat.edu.in",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 6. Set Authentication Token Variable
@authToken = {{login.response.body.token}}

### 7. Seed Task in MongoDB (Write Operation)
# @name createTask
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Evaluate In-Memory Caching Latency",
  "description": "Practical 9 node-cache TTL benchmark with Express and MongoDB",
  "priority": "high",
  "completed": false
}

### 8. First Request: Cache MISS (Queries MongoDB & Stores in Cache)
# Check response header: X-Cache should be "MISS"
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 9. Second Request: Cache HIT (Immediate response from node-cache)
# Check response header: X-Cache should be "HIT"
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 10. Third Request: Cache HIT (Confirmation of sub-millisecond retrieval)
# Check response header: X-Cache should be "HIT"
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 11. Cache Bypass via Query Parameter (?no_cache=true)
# Check response header: X-Cache should be "BYPASS"
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks?no_cache=true
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 12. Single Task Document Fetch 1: Cache MISS (Supplementary Problem 1)
@taskId = {{createTask.response.body._id}}
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 13. Single Task Document Fetch 2: Cache HIT (Supplementary Problem 1)
# Check response header: X-Cache should be "HIT"
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 14. Update Task by ID: Triggers Cache Invalidation
# Check response header: X-Cache-Invalidated should be "true"
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "completed": true,
  "priority": "medium"
}

### 15. Verify Cache MISS after Update (Ensures No Stale Data)
# Check response header: X-Cache should be "MISS"
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 16. Delete Task: Triggers Cache Invalidation
# Check response header: X-Cache-Invalidated should be "true"
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 17. Verify Cache MISS after Delete
# Check response header: X-Cache should be "MISS"
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 18. Inspect Final Cache Statistics & Hit Ratio
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cache/stats
Accept: application/json

### 19. Unauthorized Request Test (Expected: 401 Unauthorized)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Accept: application/json

### 20. 404 Route Not Found Test
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/unknown-endpoint
Accept: application/json

### 21. 500 Internal Server Error Simulation
GET {{baseUrl}}/error-test
Accept: application/json
